Recovered 324 partial snapshots, the last one being:

🍕 Classic Margherita Pizza

Ingredients
-----------
  • 2 cups all-purpose flour
  • 1 teaspoon active dry yeast
  • 3/4 cup warm water
  • 1 teaspoon salt
  • 1 teaspoon sugar
  • 1 tablespoon olive oil
  • 1/2 cup tomato sauce
  • 1 1/2 cups fresh mozzarella cheese, sliced
  • Fresh basil leaves
  • Salt to taste
  • Olive oil for drizzling

Steps
-----
  1. In a bowl, mix warm water, yeast, and sugar. Let it sit for about 5 minutes until frothy.
  2. In another bowl, combine flour and salt. Create a well in the center and pour in the yeast mixture and olive oil.
  3. Mix until a dough forms, then knead on a floured surface for about 10 minutes until smooth.
  4. Place the dough in a greased bowl, cover with a damp cloth, and let it rise in a warm place for about 1 hour, or until doubled in size.
  5. Preheat the oven to its highest setting (usually around 475°F or 245°C). If using a pizza stone, place it in the oven to preheat.
  6. Punch down the risen dough and roll it out on a floured surface into a 12-inch circle.
  7. Transfer the dough to a pizza peel or baking sheet. Spread the tomato sauce evenly over the base.
  8. Lay the mozzarella slices over the sauce and sprinkle a little salt on top.
  9. Bake in the preheated oven (preferably on the pizza stone) for about 10-12 minutes or until the crust is golden and the cheese is bubbly.
  10. Remove from the oven and add fresh basil leaves and a drizzle of olive oil before slicing and serving.
